IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voca-schedules`
IMPORT `voca-core`
IMPORT `voca-seat-funeral`
IMPORT `voca-seat`

-- Cases for the seat of the person who paid for a victim's funeral (voca-seat-funeral.l4), the funeral regulative
-- rules of the core, and MIRROR cases: the same facts asked from the victim's seat (voca-seat.l4), with answers that
-- agree. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited Act (REPV014), never copied from the encoding's
-- output. HYPOTHETICAL people throughout; no scenario life covers the Northern Territory.
--
-- Eligibility answers, in order: a criminal act in the NT; a criminal offence or excused; against the person who died
-- (or they died trying to stop it, help or arrest); died as a direct result; I paid or will likely pay; I committed it.

`1 Jul 2025` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025
`1 Sep 2025` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 1. Can I apply (ss 47A, 47B)?
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Rosa paid for the funeral of her brother, stabbed to death in Alice Springs: yes.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for funeral expense assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The brother's partner, who killed him and paid for the funeral: no (s 47B(2)).
#ASSERT `Can I apply for funeral expense assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- He died later of an unrelated illness, not as a direct result: no. The stabbing was in Queensland: no. It was no
-- offence (an accident): no. Rosa has not paid and is not likely to pay: no.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for funeral expense assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for funeral expense assistance` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for funeral expense assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for funeral expense assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A pedestrian killed by a driver who deliberately ran her down (an offence; a motor accident the MAC Act covers): ss
-- 17-18 reach only interim payments and awards, so her funeral payer can still apply (finding 11).
#ASSERT `Can I apply for funeral expense assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 2. Am I in time (s 47C)?
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Death 10 May 2025: in time to 10 May 2027 (READING: "within 2 years after" ends on the second anniversary); the day
-- after is late, so the Director must accept it under s 47C(2).
#ASSERT `Is my funeral application in time` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 5 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 5 2027) EQUALS `in time: within 2 years after the death (s 47C(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my funeral application in time` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 5 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 11 5 2027) EQUALS `late: the Director may accept it only if the Director considers the circumstances justify it (s 47C(2))`
-- Death on 29 February 2024: READING, the period ends 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Is my funeral application in time` (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026) EQUALS `in time: within 2 years after the death (s 47C(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my funeral application in time` (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) EQUALS `late: the Director may accept it only if the Director considers the circumstances justify it (s 47C(2))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 3. How much (ss 47B(4), 47D, 47E(2))? After the six eligibility answers: date of death; date applied; the
-- Director accepts it late; reasonable costs; paid by an organisation; already paid to me; already paid to others.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Rosa's reasonable costs 12 000, nothing else paid: the lesser of 12 000 and 15 000: 12 000.
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` FALSE 12000 0 0 0 EQUALS `the most funeral expense assistance I can be paid now, in dollars, is` 12000
-- Costs 20 000, a funeral insurer paid 3 000: lesser of 17 000 and 15 000: 15 000. Insurer paid 8 000: 12 000.
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` FALSE 20000 3000 0 0 EQUALS `the most funeral expense assistance I can be paid now, in dollars, is` 15000
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` FALSE 20000 8000 0 0 EQUALS `the most funeral expense assistance I can be paid now, in dollars, is` 12000
-- The pedestrian's funeral, costs 9 000, a motor accidents funeral benefit of 6 000 paid by the insurer (an
-- organisation): 3 000.
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` FALSE 9000 6000 0 0 EQUALS `the most funeral expense assistance I can be paid now, in dollars, is` 3000
-- A second payment to Rosa (s 47B(4)): costs 12 000, 5 000 already paid to her: lesser of 7 000 and 10 000: 7 000.
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` FALSE 12000 0 5000 0 EQUALS `the most funeral expense assistance I can be paid now, in dollars, is` 7000
-- Two payers: Rosa's costs 10 000; her father was already paid 9 000 for the same funeral. READING, one $15 000 per
-- funeral (finding 15): lesser of 10 000 and 6 000: 6 000.
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` FALSE 10000 0 0 9000 EQUALS `the most funeral expense assistance I can be paid now, in dollars, is` 6000
-- The insurer paid more than the costs: nothing.
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` FALSE 5000 7000 0 0 EQUALS `the most funeral expense assistance I can be paid now, in dollars, is` 0
-- Death 1 January 2023, application 1 February 2026: late. Not accepted: none (s 47E(2)(b)). Accepted: 12 000.
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2023) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) FALSE 12000 0 0 0 EQUALS `none: the application is late and the Director has not accepted it (ss 47C, 47E(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2023) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) TRUE 12000 0 0 0 EQUALS `the most funeral expense assistance I can be paid now, in dollars, is` 12000
-- The partner who killed him: none.
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` FALSE 12000 0 0 0 EQUALS `none: I am not eligible to apply (s 47B)`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 4. Payment and refund (ss 47F, 47G), with the regulative rules. Clock: days.
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Within how many days must my funeral assistance be paid` EQUALS 28
-- s 47F: the Director decides on day 0 to pay Rosa 12 000; paid day 28: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 29, 45, 46(10), 47F -- the Territory must pay within 28 days` `funeral expense assistance (s 47F)` 12000) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Territory` (`pay the amount specified in the notice` 12000) 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the Territory, "s 47F: the Territory must pay funeral expense assistance no later than 28 days ..."
#TRACE `ss 29, 45, 46(10), 47F -- the Territory must pay within 28 days` `funeral expense assistance (s 47F)` 12000 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Territory` DOES `pay the amount specified in the notice` 12000 AT 29

-- s 47G: the funeral insurer later pays 2 000 (s 47G(1)(b)); the Director requires a refund of 2 000 with a notice
-- giving 21 days: READING, at least 28 days after receipt. A notice giving 35: 35.
#ASSERT `How long do I have to refund funeral assistance` 21 EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `How long do I have to refund funeral assistance` 35 EQUALS 35
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 47, 47G -- a person required to refund must refund within the time in the notice` `a refund of funeral expense assistance (s 47G)` 2000 21) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person required to refund` (`refund the amount to the Territory` 2000) 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the person required to refund, "s 47G(2)(c), (3): ... it is a debt owing to the Territory" (day 35)
#TRACE `ss 47, 47G -- a person required to refund must refund within the time in the notice` `a refund of funeral expense assistance (s 47G)` 2000 21 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person required to refund` DOES `refund the amount to the Territory` 2000 AT 35

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 5. Closure, review and costs, with MIRROR cases from the victim's seat (the same facts, the same answers).
-- NTCAT time: HYPOTHETICAL 28 days (the NTCAT Act is not deposited).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Closure: notice 1 March 2026, no reply, Rosa asks on 15 April 2026 (within 6 months of the 31 March closure): the
-- Director must reopen it (s 47K).
#ASSERT `Is my funeral application open or closed` TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 4 2026) EQUALS `closed, and the Director must reopen it: I asked within 6 months of the closure (s 47K)`
#ASSERT `Is my funeral application open or closed` TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 4 2026) EQUALS `Is my application open or closed` TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 4 2026)

-- Review: the Director's decision on her application, 10 days ago: item 4. A refund requirement: item 5. 30 days ago:
-- past the time given.
#ASSERT `Can I seek NTCAT review of the funeral decision` `the Director's decision on my application for funeral expense assistance` 10 28 EQUALS `yes: I may apply to NTCAT for review (s 48(3)), within the NTCAT Act time I gave` 4
#ASSERT `Can I seek NTCAT review of the funeral decision` `the Director's decision requiring me to refund funeral expense assistance` 10 28 EQUALS `yes: I may apply to NTCAT for review (s 48(3)), within the NTCAT Act time I gave` 5
#ASSERT `Can I seek NTCAT review of the funeral decision` `the Director's decision on my application for funeral expense assistance` 30 28 EQUALS `I am the affected person (s 48(2)), but the NTCAT Act time I gave has passed` 4
#ASSERT `Can I seek NTCAT review of the funeral decision` `the Director's decision on my application for funeral expense assistance` 10 28 EQUALS `Can I apply for NTCAT review` `the Director's decision under s 47E on an application for funeral expense assistance` TRUE 10 28
#ASSERT `Can I seek NTCAT review of the funeral decision` `the Director's decision requiring me to refund funeral expense assistance` 10 28 EQUALS `Can I apply for NTCAT review` `the Director's decision under s 47G(1) requiring a refund of funeral expense assistance` TRUE 10 28

-- Costs: disbursements 900, counsel 300: 600 (s 54(2)-(3)); 200 without counsel: 200.
#ASSERT `What can my lawyer charge me for the funeral application` 900 300 EQUALS `the most the legal practitioner may recover from me, in dollars, is` 600
#ASSERT `What can my lawyer charge me for the funeral application` 200 0 EQUALS `the most the legal practitioner may recover from me, in dollars, is` 200
#ASSERT `What can my lawyer charge me for the funeral application` 900 300 EQUALS `What can my lawyer charge me` `an application for funeral expense assistance (Division 5A)` 900 300
